@startuml
title III-07 - Customer checkout, PayOS payment and abandoned-order handling

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer
boundary "Customer Portal" as Web
control "Order Service / API" as API
database "CRM Database" as DB
participant "PayOS API" as PayOS
participant "Expiry / Abandoned-order Scheduler" as Job

== Checkout transaction ==
Customer -> Web: Confirm selected items, address and payment method
Web -> API: POST /api/orders\n(items, deliveryAddress, paymentMethod, optional voucherCode)
API -> DB: Lock products; validate variants and available stock
alt Invalid items or insufficient stock
  API --> Web: 400 INVALID_CART / 409 OUT_OF_STOCK
else Valid checkout
  API -> DB: Deduct stock and create order items in transaction
  API -> API: Prepare order.status=PENDING and unique orderCode
  opt Voucher supplied
    API -> DB: Lock voucher; validate eligibility and limits\nincrement used_count and set discount_amount
  end
  API -> API: totalAmount=max(subtotal-discountAmount, 0)
  API -> DB: Save order and optional voucher_usages record\nreleased_at=NULL; consume purchased cart quantities
  API -> DB: Create ORDER_CREATED in-app notification
  alt Total amount is zero
    API -> DB: Set order.paymentStatus=PAID and payment.status=PAID
  else Payment method is COD
    API -> DB: Set order.paymentStatus=COD and payment.status=PENDING
  else Payment method is PAYOS and amount is positive
    API -> DB: Set order.paymentStatus=PENDING\nexpires_at=now+15 minutes
    API -> PayOS: Create payment link\ncanonical totalAmount as exact integer VND
    PayOS --> API: checkoutUrl, paymentLinkId, qrCode
    API -> DB: Save payment and payment_attempts
  end
  API -> DB: Commit checkout transaction
  API --> Web: 201 Checkout(order, optional paymentUrl and QR)
  opt PayOS link returned
    Web --> Customer: Show QR / open checkoutUrl
    Customer -> PayOS: Complete payment
  end
end
note over API,DB
  Checkout exceptions roll back local order, stock and voucher writes.
  Voucher usage is recorded at checkout; there is no
  RESERVED/CONFIRMED voucher-state column or webhook finalization.
  Optional order emails run after commit only when Resend is configured.
end note

== Return/cancel URL is display only ==
PayOS --> Web: Redirect returnUrl/cancelUrl with payment result
Web -> API: GET /api/payments/payos/return
API --> Web: Display-only result; no order-state transition

== Webhook transaction ==
PayOS -> API: POST /api/payments/payos/webhook\npayload and signature
API -> API: Verify signature; resolve attempt/orderCode
API -> DB: Lock order; verify amount and paymentLinkId
alt Invalid signature, order or amount/link mismatch
  API --> PayOS: 400 INVALID_WEBHOOK
else Valid matching PAYOS payment
  alt Order already PAID or CANCELLED
    API -> API: Handle duplicate or late payment
    opt Additional successful payment / success after cancellation
      API -> DB: Record PAID; flag multiple payments for review\nor request manual cancellation refund as applicable
    end
  else Order still eligible for payment update
    API -> DB: Check event_key and record new webhook event
    alt Duplicate event
      API -> API: No-op
    else success=true and data.code=00
      API -> DB: Set payment/attempt PAID and order.paymentStatus=PAID
      API -> DB: Create payment notification; keep order.status unchanged
    else Payment did not succeed
      API -> DB: Mark attempt EXPIRED or CANCELLED
      opt Callback belongs to current payment link
        API -> DB: Update payment and order.paymentStatus\ncreate PAYMENT_FAILED notification
      end
      API -> API: Keep order.status and stock/voucher reservation
    end
  end
  API -> DB: Commit payment update
  API --> PayOS: 200 success=true
end
note over API,DB
  Successful payment does not move order.status to CONFIRMED.
  Manager confirms the order separately.
  Expired/failed attempts may be retried or synchronized by Customer.
end note

== Link expiry is separate from order cancellation ==
Job -> API: cleanupExpired (default every 300000 ms)
API -> DB: Lock expired PAYOS orders with paymentStatus=PENDING
API -> DB: Mark payment/attempt and order.paymentStatus=EXPIRED\ncreate PAYMENT_EXPIRED notification
API -> API: Keep order.status and reserved stock/voucher

== Optional abandoned-order cancellation ==
Job -> API: AbandonedOrderScheduler (default every 300000 ms)
alt PAYOS_AUTO_CANCEL_ENABLED=false (default)
  API -> API: Skip automatic cancellation
else Enabled; latest order/payment/attempt expiry plus grace elapsed
  API -> DB: Lock candidate order (PENDING or legacy PENDING_PAYMENT)
  API -> PayOS: Reconcile all links; cancel open links and verify result
  PayOS --> API: Provider payment state
  alt Confirmed UNPAID
    API -> DB: Set order and payment CANCELLED\nrelease stock and voucher once; create ORDER_AUTO_CANCELLED
  else Paid, mismatch, provider error or review required
    API -> DB: Record payment/review result; keep stock and voucher
  end
end
note over Job,DB
  Grace defaults to 24 hours after the latest expiry, range 1-720 hours.
  Demo explicitly enables automatic cancellation; code defaults to false.
  PayOS real-transaction testing is still pending and will be
  performed separately with authorized transactions.
end note
@enduml
